id: B03
target: src/sello/private/backend.nim
desc: signDetached: RFC 8032 5.1.6 step 2 nonce derivation r = SHA-512(prefix || msg) computed as SHA-512(msg || prefix) instead -- the two-part hash's argument order swapped, corrupting the per-message nonce r (and therefore R = [r]B and S = k*a + r) for every message except the degenerate empty-prefix-or-empty-msg case. Re-anchored (RFC-006 slice 3): the swap onto the in-house `sha512` one-shot collapsed the `nonceSha.init()`/`update`(x2)/`finish()` streaming sequence this mutant's OLD text targeted into one `sha512(prefix, msg)` call expression -- the OLD/NEW pair here was updated to match the new source text verbatim while preserving the identical argument-order-swap defect class, the same re-anchoring register as F23's precedent.
====OLD====
    nonceHash = sha512(prefix, msg)
====NEW====
    nonceHash = sha512(msg, prefix)
====END====
